=== PARITY (vs web FSMDistributionWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (FSMDistributionSource ->
    FSMDistributionModel): useFSMStats, useFSMTransitions, useVehicles, useTranslation. The production
    app wires the source over the shared FSM-stats/-transitions stores (vehicle resolved as the web
    `vehicleId ?? vehicles[0].id`); the view performs NO HTTP.
  Projection -> FSMDonutBuilder is a 1:1 port of buildDonutData (drop non-positive durations, total,
    per-state pct, sort largest-first, empty => []); FSMDuration.format ports fmtDuration (Nm under an
    hour else Nh Nm, units via t()); FSMStatePalette ports STATE_COLORS with the case-insensitive
    lookup + gray fallback and the EXACT web hex (#22d3ee/#22c55e/#a855f7/#f59e0b/#6b7280);
    FSMTransitionBuilder ports the feed (newest-first, from/to '—' fallbacks, capped at 5 = web per_page).
    All verified by swiftc-typechecked XCTest (28 methods).
  Composition -> shell chrome (state-graph icon + "State Distribution" title + freshness chip + refresh
    + optional Open) · 1x2 compact (state dot + localized state name + time-in-state) · 2x4 standard
    (SectorMark donut + legend row[state swatch + localized name + pct + time] + "Recent Transitions"
    feed of from->to chips + relative time). isCompact = size.cols <= 1 (web parity).
  Charts -> web Recharts PieChart (innerRadius 55% / outerRadius 80% / paddingAngle 2) => Swift Charts
    SectorMark (innerRadius .ratio(0.55) / angularInset 2). Web hover tooltip (duration + pct) has no
    touch equivalent, so the always-visible legend carries state+pct+time and the donut speaks one
    VoiceOver summary — no slice value is hidden behind an unavailable hover affordance.

=== STATES (all rendered) ===
  loading  -> skeleton chrome (donut block + legend bars [+ feed rows on standard])
